## Phase 1 — Get the block on screen

**Find an existing preview route first:**

```bash
grep -rn "blocks/" src/app --include="*.tsx" -l | head
ls src/app 2>/dev/null
```

**If none exists, use a scratch route** — and delete it when done:

```tsx
// src/app/__audit/page.tsx  — TEMPORARY, delete before finishing
import Block from "@/components/uiable/blocks/<category>/<block-name>/<block-name>"

export default function AuditPage() {
  return <Block />
}
```

> **The scratch route must not survive the audit.** It imports a block into the app's routable tree; left behind it ships as a real page. Delete it in Phase 6 and confirm `ls src/app/__audit` returns nothing. If the run is interrupted, deleting this is the first thing to do on resume.

Boot it and drive it with whatever browser tooling the session has — the `run` skill can launch the app and capture screenshots if no browser tool is wired directly. Write every screenshot to the **scratchpad**, never into the repo.

```bash
npm run dev    # background; note the port, it is not always 3000
```

